---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import {SUPPORT_EMAIL} from '../lib/site';

const sections = [
  {id: 'agreement', title: 'Using the service'},
  {id: 'accounts', title: 'Your account'},
  {id: 'content', title: 'Your content and permissions'},
  {id: 'public', title: 'Public snippets and third-party content'},
  {id: 'acceptable-use', title: 'Acceptable use'},
  {id: 'backups', title: 'Synchronization and backups'},
  {id: 'availability', title: 'Availability and changes'},
  {id: 'termination', title: 'Suspension and closing your account'},
  {id: 'disclaimers', title: 'Disclaimers and responsibility'},
  {id: 'disputes', title: 'Disputes and legal rights'},
  {id: 'updates', title: 'Changes to these terms'},
  {id: 'contact', title: 'Contact'},
];
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms for using Command Snippets, operated by Tearleads, LLC: accounts, content ownership, public sharing, acceptable use, backups and your legal rights."
  sections={sections}
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p class="lede">
      These terms govern your use of the Command Snippets website, web app and
      API, provided by Tearleads, LLC (“we,” “us” or “our”).
    </p>
    <p>
      Please read these terms and our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>{' '}
      before using the service. Questions can be sent to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <h2 id="agreement">1. Using the service</h2>
  <p>
    By creating an account or using Command Snippets, you agree to these terms.
    If you do not agree, do not use the service. You must be at least 18 and
    legally able to enter into this agreement. If you use the service for an
    organization, you must have authority to agree on its behalf.
  </p>
  <p>
    Command Snippets helps you save, organize, copy and optionally share text
    snippets. We give you permission to use the service in accordance with these
    terms. The service's software, branding and other materials remain owned by
    Tearleads, LLC or their respective owners; these terms do not transfer those
    rights to you. Separate open-source licenses continue to apply where provided.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accounts">2. Your account</h2>
  <p>
    Sign-in uses Google or GitHub. Keep your identity-provider account and devices
    secure, provide accurate account information, and notify us if you suspect
    unauthorized access. You are responsible for activity you authorize through
    your account. Third-party sign-in services have their own terms and policies;
    losing access to them may affect access to Command Snippets.
  </p>

  <h2 id="content">3. Your content and permissions</h2>
  <p>
    You retain your rights in the snippets and other content you submit. You
    must have permission to store and share that content, including any material
    belonging to an employer, client or other person.
  </p>
  <p>
    You grant Tearleads, LLC a nonexclusive permission to host, store, reproduce,
    transmit and display your content only as needed to provide, maintain and
    secure the service, follow your sharing choices, and meet legal obligations.
    This includes using service providers for those purposes. It does not give
    us ownership of your content or permission to use private snippets in advertising.
    After deletion or account closure, this permission continues only for retained
    copies and purposes described in the Privacy Policy or required by law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="public">4. Public snippets and third-party content</h2>
  <p>
    Snippets and tags start private. Making a snippet and a tag containing it
    public allows other people to view and copy that snippet. Publish only
    content you have the right to share. Making content private or deleting it
    cannot remove copies already made by others.
  </p>
  <p>
    Public availability is not a promise that content is accurate, safe or licensed
    for every use. Respect any applicable licenses and obtain permission when
    needed. Review commands before running them; a snippet may delete data,
    expose credentials or behave differently on your system. Command Snippets
    does not test or guarantee commands copied from the service.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">5. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You must not use the service to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Violate applicable law or another person's privacy, intellectual property or other rights.</li>
    <li>Publish stolen credentials, private personal information, malicious code intended to harm others, or unlawful content.</li>
    <li>Access another person's account or private content without authorization, bypass access controls, or impersonate someone.</li>
    <li>Disrupt the service, overload its infrastructure, evade restrictions or use it to distribute spam.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Good-faith security reports are welcome at{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>. Do not access or
    disclose other people's data while investigating. These terms do not
    restrict conduct that applicable law protects.
  </p>

  <h2 id="backups">6. Synchronization and backups</h2>
  <p>
    Edits save on your device before they synchronize. Offline changes may not
    reach the server until you reconnect; clearing browser data or discarding
    pending changes can permanently lose them. Keep independent backups of
    important content using the app's export feature.
  </p>
  <p>
    Restoring a backup creates a new data version. Earlier versions remain until
    deleted, and switching versions may discard edits that have not synchronized
    from other devices. Read the app's confirmation messages before restoring,
    switching versions or clearing data. The service is not a substitute for
    your own backup or recovery process.
  </p>

  <h2 id="availability">7. Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may maintain, update or change features, set reasonable usage limits, or
    discontinue the service. We do not promise uninterrupted access or that
    every feature will remain available. Where reasonably practicable, we will
    give advance notice of a discontinuation or material reduction in access
    and an opportunity to export your data. Urgent security, abuse or legal
    issues may require immediate action.
  </p>
  <p>
    These terms do not authorize charges. If we introduce paid features, their
    prices and payment terms will be presented separately before you choose them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="termination">8. Suspension and closing your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using the service at any time. To close your account or request
    deletion, email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
    Signing out or revoking Google or GitHub access does not itself delete your
    account or stored content. Export anything you want to keep first.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may restrict or suspend access or remove content when reasonably necessary
    to address a breach of these terms, security risks, unlawful activity or a
    legal requirement. When appropriate, we will explain the reason and allow
    you to contact us to resolve it. Data retention and deletion are described
    in the <a href="/privacy/#retention">Privacy Policy</a>. Provisions that
    by their nature need to continue, including ownership and dispute provisions,
    remain applicable after you stop using the service.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimers">9. Disclaimers and responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by applicable law, the service is provided “as is”
    and “as available,” without implied warranties of merchantability, fitness
    for a particular purpose or noninfringement. We do not guarantee that the
    service or user content will be error-free, secure in every circumstance,
    or suitable for a particular workflow.
  </p>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by applicable law, Tearleads, LLC is not liable for
    indirect or consequential losses, including lost profits or business
    opportunities, arising from use of the service. This does not exclude or
    limit liability for fraud, intentional misconduct, gross negligence, or any
    other liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited. Your mandatory
    consumer rights and remedies remain intact.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disputes">10. Disputes and legal rights</h2>
  <p>
    Please contact us first so we can try to resolve concerns informally. This
    does not prevent you from contacting a regulator, seeking urgent relief or
    pursuing any remedy available under applicable law. These terms do not
    require arbitration or waive class-action rights.
  </p>
  <p>
    Applicable law governs your rights and obligations. Nothing in these terms
    removes protections or access to courts that mandatory law gives you. If a
    provision is unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue to apply to
    the extent permitted by law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="updates">11. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may revise these terms and will update the date on this page. For material
    changes, we will provide notice through the service or another appropriate
    channel before they take effect, unless an urgent legal or security reason
    requires otherwise. Changes apply prospectively. If you do not agree to
    revised terms, stop using the service and contact us about exporting your
    data and closing your account. We will request affirmative agreement when
    required by applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Command Snippets is operated by Tearleads, LLC. For support, questions about
    these terms, or reports of content that infringes your rights, email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>. Include the relevant
    page or snippet link and a description of the issue; do not send passwords
    or access tokens.
  </p>
</Legal>
